<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The wings every winged caste wears: one attachment node, drawing VRE Insector's
		insect wing art behind her in her caste's colour - the same palette her hair, her
		spider legs and her abdomen wear (rolled by Source/Insects/InsectColours.cs).

		This is a copy of VRE's own `VRE_InsectWings_Cosmetic`, and the copy is the whole
		point. Their gene carries the exclusion tag `InsectorMovement`, and so do
		`VRE_HardLockedJoints` (the abaddon queen's degrade), `VRE_InflexibleJoints` and
		`VRE_LocustWings`. Two genes that share a tag are conflicting genes to the engine,
		and `Pawn_GeneTracker.CheckForOverrides` - which runs from every `AddGene` -
		silences one of the pair (user's report, 2026-10-04: the queen's wings or her
		joints were being overridden by a tag about movement that has nothing to do with
		a cosmetic pair of wings). The tag lives on their def, so the fix is a def of
		ours with no tags.

		Patching their def instead was rejected the way B&S's spider body was: the tag is
		theirs, and every insector in a save would have felt the change (SpiderBody_BS.xml
		records the same trade, user's call 2026-10-01). The art is still theirs, by path
		- the same dependency the old arrangement had, since the texture came from their
		mod either way. The two stat-carrying wing genes (`VRE_InsectWings`,
		`VRE_LocustWings`) stay out of every caste package as before: they grant movement
		and an ability, and the castes' own flight genes own that ground (archive/HANDOFF.md
		§5.22).

		No exclusion tags at all, deliberately: a tag is the bug this def exists to avoid.
		Nothing else of ours carries wings, and the real VRE wing genes are kept out by
		the caste lists rather than by a tag.
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_CosmeticWings</defName>
		<label>insect wings, cosmetic</label>
		<description>She grows a pair of insect wings at her back. They are looks alone - whatever carries her through the air is her own flight gene's work.</description>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_InsectWings</iconPath>
		<displayCategory>Movement</displayCategory>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1000</displayOrderInCategory>
		<!-- Cosmetic: costs nothing in the xenotype editor. -->
		<biostatCpx>0</biostatCpx>
		<biostatMet>0</biostatMet>
		<!-- Out of the random genepacks, like every other gene of ours: a pack should not
		     hand a stranger the family's wings piecemeal. -->
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<!-- Copied from VRE's gene, so the art lands exactly where it always did: a vanilla
		     attachment node on the Body tag, behind her (-2) except in the north view (90),
		     scaled with body size, with the east and west offsets that set the pair
		     off-centre as their own pawns wear it. The colour line is NOT theirs: VRE tints
		     by skin (`colorType Skin` + `useSkinShader`), and the wings wear the caste's own
		     colour instead - `colorType Hair`, because the palette is rolled into her hair
		     (Source/Insects/InsectColours.cs). The skin shader had to go with it: it draws
		     the sprite from the pawn's skin whatever `colorType` says. What is left is
		     field for field what vanilla's own hair-tinted tail is (Biotech's FurryTail:
		     same worker, same tag, same layer, `colorType Hair`, no shader at all). -->
		<renderNodeProperties>
			<li>
				<workerClass>PawnRenderNodeWorker_AttachmentBody</workerClass>
				<texPath>Things/Pawn/Humanlike/BodyAttachments/Insectwings</texPath>
				<drawSize>1</drawSize>
				<parentTagDef>Body</parentTagDef>
				<colorType>Hair</colorType>
				<useRottenColor>true</useRottenColor>
				<rotDrawMode>Fresh, Rotting</rotDrawMode>
				<drawData>
					<defaultData><layer>-2</layer></defaultData>
					<scaleOffsetByBodySize>true</scaleOffsetByBodySize>
					<dataNorth><layer>90</layer></dataNorth>
					<dataEast><offset>(-0.2, 0, 0)</offset></dataEast>
					<dataWest><offset>(0.2, 0, 0)</offset></dataWest>
				</drawData>
			</li>
		</renderNodeProperties>
	</GeneDef>
</Defs>
